// The console's server: accounts, sessions and verified leaderboards, for every wrela game
// (games/capybara/design.md, "Accounts and leaderboards"). The console's program runs it as its
// server build, on Cloudflare (toolchain 0.13.0's host: a Durable Object holds the instance and its
// store), answering HTTP requests to wrela.dev's `/api/` (wire.wrela). A game reaches it only through
// the console (link.wrela), since a server takes only its own program's clients
// (docs/toolchain-gaps.md, "A server takes one program's clients").
//
// It is a state machine over its host, so tests can run it on a fake store: what it asks of the
// host comes out as `Command`s (the store's reads and writes, random bytes, a signature to check,
// the responses), and the host's answers go back in by their ticket (`answer`). The console's
// `serve` (console_server) carries the commands out through std::store, std::crypto and std::http,
// one call at a time; a read is answered on the call after the one that asked, and the host commits
// a call's writes when it returns, before its responses go.
//
// **A request is a short connection**: it opens, gives its one request (`http`), and takes one
// response. Every request is answered: one whose work ends without a reply is refused at the end of
// the call (`end`). Its session is the `__Host-session` cookie, read again on each request.
//
// What it keeps is in the store (account.wrela's keys), never only in memory: the host may drop the
// instance between requests, and does after a failed call. A ceremony's challenge is kept in the
// store too, under the token of the browser that asked for it (its `__Host-ceremony` cookie), so it
// is used once, by that browser. In memory are only what may be lost: the requests under way, which
// ceremonies and names were used in calls whose writes a read may not yet see, a limit on recovery
// tries across everyone (the host limits each client: docs/toolchain.md), the run being verified, and
// which requests wait for their uploads.
//
// **Passkeys** (WebAuthn Level 3, §7, through std::webauthn; the signature through std::crypto):
// every check the design asks for. A credential belongs to one account; an assertion is taken only
// for its credential's account, and with the account's handle when the browser gives one.
//
// **Runs** are verified by playing them again on the board's build (the game's `Game`): the server
// works out the time and the category itself, and refuses a run whose claim the rules can't make.
// An upload is bounded (its bytes, its ticks, an account's runs an hour, the queue's length), and
// the queue plays one run at a time, `PLAY_TICKS` ticks a call, so a run an attacker chose holds up
// the server's other requests a bounded time each call. The queue is in the store, so it goes on
// after the instance is dropped; the upload's request is answered when its run is.
//
// **The clock** is the host's wall clock: each request's time (`Asked::time`), never going back
// while the instance runs. Work no request waits on (the queue) needs no time.

use account::{
    Account, CHALLENGE_BYTES, CHALLENGE_LIFE, CODES, CODE_BYTES, CSRF_BYTES, FRESH, GameToken,
    HANDLE_BYTES, HOUR, MINUTE, MOST_PASSKEYS, OF_BEST, OF_CODE, OF_HOUR, OF_PASSKEY, OF_RUN,
    OF_SEEN, OF_SESSION, OF_TOKEN, Passkey, REROLLS, Recovery, SESSION_LIFE, Session, TOKEN_BYTES,
    TOKEN_LIFE, account_key, ceremonies, ceremony_key, code, code_hash, code_key, hashed, hex,
    indexed, name_key, passkey_key, public_id, session_key, token_key, u32_at, u64_at,
    under_account, CEREMONY_BYTES,
}
use names::{Name, draw}
use std::collections::replace
use std::crypto::{Signature, verified}
use std::fmt::json_text
use std::serialize::{LoadError, Serialize, load, save}
use std::store::{append_u32, append_u64, entries, past, value}
use std::webauthn::{Credential, Expected, assertion, base64url, registration}
use wire::{
    ADD_PASSKEY, ANY, BOARD_PAGE, EXPORT_PART, FULL, MOST_REPLAY, Me, PasskeyView, Place, REGISTER,
    Reply, Request, SIGN_IN, SessionView, WHOLE,
}

// ---- what a game gives the server ----------------------------------------------------------------

/// What a replay says it is, read without playing it: its course and its time in ticks.
pub struct Claim: Copy {
    pub course: u32,
    pub ticks: u32,
}

/// What playing a replay made of it: its time, and whether it counts for 100%.
pub struct Outcome: Copy {
    pub ticks: u32,
    pub full: bool,
}

/// A game's boards: its name, its board's version (its build of play: a change to play starts a
/// new one, games/capybara/design.md, "Physics is locked at release"), its courses, and how to
/// check a replay.
pub trait Game {
    /// A replay being played.
    type Run

    /// The game's key (`capybara`), as its catalog names it.
    fn id(self) -> Text

    /// The board version this build verifies for.
    fn board(self) -> u32

    /// How many courses have boards: courses 0 to this, less one.
    fn courses(self) -> u32

    /// What `replay` claims, if it reads as one of the game's replays and is within its bounds
    /// (its course, its length): `Err` says why not, for a person.
    fn claim(self, replay: [u8]) -> Result<Claim, Text>

    /// A replay that `claim` took, ready to play.
    fn start(self, replay: [u8]) -> Self::Run

    /// Plays at most `ticks` more ticks of `run`: none until it has played all of it, then what it
    /// came to, or why its claim isn't what the rules make of it.
    fn play(self, run: mut Self::Run, ticks: u32) -> Option<Result<Outcome, Text>>
}

// ---- bounds --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// Runs an account may upload an hour.
pub const RUNS_AN_HOUR: u32 = 10
/// Runs waiting to be verified, past which an upload is refused.
pub const MOST_QUEUED: u32 = 32
/// Ticks of a run played a call. The capybara's sim took about 12 µs a tick on wrela-serve
/// (docs/bench.md, "The console's server"), so this is about 5 ms a call: the server's other
/// requests wait no longer than that behind a run, and a call stays far inside Workers Paid's CPU
/// time (30 s an invocation: developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/platform/limits/).
pub const PLAY_TICKS: u32 = 400
/// Recovery codes everyone may try in a minute. Each client's own limit is the host's, by address
/// (`WRELA_LIMITS`, studio/release), which the server is never told.
pub const ALL_TRIES: u32 = 30
/// How long a public read may be kept by a cache, in seconds: a board's page (it changes as runs
/// come), and a run's replay (it never does).
pub const BOARD_AGE: u32 = 30
pub const RUN_AGE: u32 = 86400
/// The ceremonies and names used lately, which a read made before their call's writes committed
/// wouldn't see as used.
pub const MOST_RECENT: u32 = 64
/// Expired ceremonies cleared as a new one begins.
pub const PRUNED: u32 = 16
/// The most places a run's place is counted to.
pub const MOST_PLACE: u32 = 1000

// ---- what the server asks of its host ------------------------------------------------------------

pub enum Command: Clone {
    Get { ticket: u32, key: Vec<u8> },
    Scan { ticket: u32, from: Vec<u8>, to: Vec<u8>, limit: u32, down: bool },
    Put { key: Vec<u8>, value: Vec<u8> },
    Delete { key: Vec<u8> },
    Random { ticket: u32, n: u32 },
    Verify {
        ticket: u32,
        algorithm: Signature,
        key: Vec<u8>,
        message: Vec<u8>,
        signature: Vec<u8>,
    },
    /// The one answer to request `conn`: a `Reply`'s bytes, the cookies it sets, and how long a
    /// cache may keep it (0: none may).
    Respond { conn: u32, body: Vec<u8>, cookies: Vec<Cookie>, public: u32 },
}

/// A first-party session cookie (`std::http::session_cookie`): `__Host-<name>`, holding `value`,
/// for `max_age` seconds (0 clears it).
pub struct Cookie: Clone {
    pub name: String,
    pub value: Vec<u8>,
    pub max_age: u32,
}

/// The session's and a ceremony's cookies.
pub const SESSION: Text = "session"
pub const CEREMONY: Text = "ceremony"

/// A request, as the host gave it: when it was taken (the host's wall clock, milliseconds since the
/// Unix epoch), whether it may be cached (a `GET`), its cookies' values, and its body (a `Request`).
pub struct Asked: Clone {
    pub time: u64,
    pub public: bool,
    pub session: Vec<u8>,
    pub ceremony: Vec<u8>,
    pub body: Vec<u8>,
}

// ---- records of runs -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// A verified run (`u/<run>`): whose, which board, its course, time and categories, and its
/// replay.
pub struct Run: Clone + Serialize {
    pub id: u64,
    pub account: u64,
    pub game: String,
    pub board: u32,
    pub course: u32,
    pub ticks: u32,
    pub full: bool,
    pub uploaded: u64,
    pub replay: Vec<u8>,
}

/// A run waiting to be verified (`q/<uploaded>/<run>`), and who to tell.
pub struct Queued: Clone + Serialize {
    pub id: u64,
    pub account: u64,
    pub name: String,
    pub game: String,
    pub board: u32,
    pub course: u32,
    pub ticks: u32,
    pub uploaded: u64,
    pub replay: Vec<u8>,
}

/// An account's best on a board (`a/<id>/b<board key>`): the run, its time, and the board's key
/// that ranks it, to replace it.
pub struct Best: Clone + Serialize {
    pub run: u64,
    pub ticks: u32,
    pub ranked: Vec<u8>,
}

/// A place on a board's ranking (`b/...`): the name it shows and the run to watch.
pub struct Ranked: Clone + Serialize {
    pub name: String,
    pub run: u64,
}

/// What an account's index entry of a run holds (`a/<id>/u<run>`): enough to show it in an export
/// without its replay.
pub struct RunIndex: Clone + Serialize {
    pub game: String,
    pub board: u32,
    pub course: u32,
    pub ticks: u32,
    pub full: bool,
    pub uploaded: u64,
}

fn text_key(p: Text) -> Vec<u8> {
    Vec::from(String::from(p).as_bytes())
}

fn push_text(k: mut Vec<u8>, s: str) {
    for i in 0..s.len() {
        k.push(s.byte(i))
    }
    k.push(0)
}

/// `u/<run>`: a run.
pub fn run_key(id: u64) -> Vec<u8> {
    var k = text_key("u/")
    append_u64(mut k, id)
    k
}

/// `q/`: the queue, oldest first.
pub fn queue_prefix() -> Vec<u8> {
    text_key("q/")
}

pub fn queue_key(at: u64, id: u64) -> Vec<u8> {
    var k = queue_prefix()
    append_u64(mut k, at)
    append_u64(mut k, id)
    k
}

/// What a board is: its game, version, course (or `WHOLE`) and category, as key bytes.
pub fn board_part(game: str, board: u32, course: u32, category: u32) -> Vec<u8> {
    var k: Vec<u8> = Vec::new()
    push_text(mut k, game)
    append_u32(mut k, board)
    append_u32(mut k, course)
    append_u32(mut k, category)
    k
}

/// `b/<board>`: a board's ranking, fastest first: `b/<board><ticks><account>`.
pub fn board_prefix(game: str, board: u32, course: u32, category: u32) -> Vec<u8> {
    var k = text_key("b/")
    for b in board_part(game, board, course, category) {
        k.push(b)
    }
    k
}

pub fn ranked_key(
    game: str,
    board: u32,
    course: u32,
    category: u32,
    ticks: u32,
    account: u64,
) -> Vec<u8> {
    var k = board_prefix(game, board, course, category)
    append_u32(mut k, ticks)
    append_u64(mut k, account)
    k
}

/// `a/<id>/b<board>`: an account's best on a board.
pub fn best_key(account: u64, game: str, board: u32, course: u32, category: u32) -> Vec<u8> {
    indexed(account, OF_BEST, board_part(game, board, course, category))
}

/// `a/<id>/b<game><version>`: the start of an account's bests on one version of a game's boards.
pub fn bests_prefix(account: u64, game: str, board: u32) -> Vec<u8> {
    var rest: Vec<u8> = Vec::new()
    push_text(mut rest, game)
    append_u32(mut rest, board)
    indexed(account, OF_BEST, rest)
}

/// `a/<id>/h<hour>`: an account's uploads in an hour of the server's clock.
pub fn rate_key(account: u64, hour: u64) -> Vec<u8> {
    var rest: Vec<u8> = Vec::new()
    append_u64(mut rest, hour)
    indexed(account, OF_HOUR, rest)
}

/// `a/<id>/d<replay's hash>`: a replay the account has uploaded, so it isn't twice.
pub fn upload_key(account: u64, replay: [u8]) -> Vec<u8> {
    indexed(account, OF_SEEN, hashed(replay))
}

// ---- the server's state ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// A ceremony a browser began (`w/...`): its challenge, and for a new account, what it will be.
struct Ceremony: Clone + Serialize {
    kind: u32,
    challenge: Vec<u8>,
    handle: Vec<u8>,
    account: u64,
    seed: u64,
    expires: u64,
}

/// A request, and the session its cookie is for.
struct Conn: Clone {
    conn: u32,
    /// Whether its request came, whether it was answered, and whether it may be cached.
    asked: bool,
    answered: bool,
    public: bool,
    /// The session's token's hash: empty when signed out.
    session: Vec<u8>,
    account: u64,
    csrf: Vec<u8>,
    fresh_until: u64,
    recovery: bool,
    /// The session's account, as the console may show it.
    me: Option<Me>,
    /// Its ceremony cookie's value, and the cookies its response sets.
    ceremony: Vec<u8>,
    cookies: Vec<Cookie>,
    /// The request, while its session cookie is read.
    pending: Option<Request>,
}

/// What a job waits for.
enum Step: Copy + Eq {
    HelloSession,
    HelloAccount,
    BeginRandom,
    BeginPrune,
    CeremonyTaken,
    BeginAddScan,
    BeginAddAccount,
    RegisterCredential,
    RegisterAccount,
    RegisterName,
    RegisterSeed,
    RegisterSecrets,
    SignInCredential,
    SignInAccount,
    SignInVerify,
    SignInSecrets,
    RecoverCode,
    RecoverAccount,
    RecoverSessions,
    RecoverSecrets,
    NameAccount,
    NameSeed,
    NameTaken,
    AddCredential,
    AddCount,
    AddSession,
    RemoveScan,
    PasskeysScan,
    CodesScan,
    CodesRandom,
    SessionsScan,
    RevokeScan,
    TokenAccount,
    TokenPrune,
    TokenRandom,
    QueueAccount,
    ExportAccount,
    ExportScan,
    ExportRun,
    DeleteAccount,
    DeleteScan,
    DeleteNext,
    UploadToken,
    UploadAccount,
    UploadRate,
    UploadSeen,
    UploadQueue,
    UploadId,
    BoardScan,
    WatchRun,
    FinishBest,
    FinishBests,
    FinishPlace,
}

/// A request under way, waiting on its ticket: what it has learned so far.
struct Job: Clone {
    conn: u32,
    ticket: u32,
    step: Step,
    request: Request,
    account: Option<Account>,
    passkey: Option<Passkey>,
    session: Option<Session>,
    credential: Option<Credential>,
    message: Vec<u8>,
    hash: Vec<u8>,
    keys: Vec<Vec<u8>>,
    views: Vec<Vec<u8>>,
    text: String,
    id: u64,
    seed: u64,
    tries: u32,
    n: u32,
    queued: Option<Queued>,
    categories: Vec<u32>,
    category: u32,
}

/// The run being verified.
struct Verifying<R> {
    key: Vec<u8>,
    queued: Queued,
    run: R,
}

/// The server.
pub struct Engine<G: Game> {
    game: G,
    rp_id: String,
    origin: String,
    out: Vec<Command>,
    ticket: u32,
    /// The server's clock: the latest request's time, in milliseconds since the Unix epoch.
    now: u64,
    conns: Vec<Conn>,
    jobs: Vec<Job>,
    /// When anyone tried a recovery code, within a minute.
    tries: Vec<u64>,
    /// The queue may hold runs; the ticket of a scan for the oldest.
    queue_waiting: bool,
    queue_scan: Option<u32>,
    /// The calls counted, and the last that wrote the queue: a read made in a call is answered
    /// from the store as it was before the call's writes (wrela_host::server), so the queue is
    /// read again only in a later call.
    call: u64,
    queue_written: u64,
    /// Names written and ceremonies used lately, which a read made before their call committed
    /// wouldn't see.
    recent_names: Vec<Vec<u8>>,
    spent: Vec<Vec<u8>>,
    /// The requests waiting for their uploads' runs to be verified: each request and its run.
    uploads: Vec<(u32, u64)>,
    verifying: Option<Verifying<G::Run>>,
    /// Whether the last call asked for nothing: then nothing would call it again, so a run being
    /// played asks the host for a byte to be called at once.
    nudge: Option<u32>,
}

/// A server for `game`'s boards, its passkeys for relying party `rp_id` from `origin` alone.
pub fn engine<G: Game>(game: take G, rp_id: str, origin: str) -> Engine<G> {
    Engine {
        game,
        rp_id: rp_id.to_string(),
        origin: origin.to_string(),
        out: Vec::new(),
        ticket: 0,
        now: 0,
        conns: Vec::new(),
        jobs: Vec::new(),
        tries: Vec::new(),
        queue_waiting: true,
        queue_scan: None,
        call: 0,
        queue_written: 0,
        recent_names: Vec::new(),
        spent: Vec::new(),
        uploads: Vec::new(),
        verifying: None,
        nudge: None,
    }
}

fn blank_job(conn: u32, request: take Request) -> Job {
    Job {
        conn,
        ticket: 0,
        step: Step::HelloSession,
        request,
        account: None,
        passkey: None,
        session: None,
        credential: None,
        message: Vec::new(),
        hash: Vec::new(),
        keys: Vec::new(),
        views: Vec::new(),
        text: String::new(),
        id: 0,
        seed: 0,
        tries: 0,
        n: 0,
        queued: None,
        categories: Vec::new(),
        category: 0,
    }
}

fn me_of(a: Account, recovery: bool) -> Me {
    Me {
        signed_in: true,
        name: names::text(a.name),
        fixed: a.fixed,
        rerolls: a.rerolls,
        must_add_passkey: recovery,
    }
}

fn nobody() -> Me {
    Me { signed_in: false, name: String::new(), fixed: false, rerolls: 0, must_add_passkey: false }
}

fn read<T: Serialize>(bytes: [u8]) -> Option<T> {
    let r: Result<T, LoadError> = load(Vec::from(bytes))
    take r.ok()
}

/// The value a `get` answered with, as a `T`: none for no value, or one that doesn't read.
fn got<T: Serialize>(answer: [u8]) -> Option<T> {
    let v = value(answer)?
    read(v)
}

/// The bytes from `at`, `n` of them.
fn part(bytes: [u8], at: u32, n: u32) -> Vec<u8> {
    var out: Vec<u8> = Vec::with_capacity(n)
    for i in at..at + n {
        out.push(bytes[i])
    }
    out
}

fn same_bytes(a: [u8], b: [u8]) -> bool {
    if a.len() != b.len() {
        return false
    }
    // Every byte is compared, whatever the first that differs, so the time says nothing of where.
    var d: u32 = 0
    for i in 0..a.len() {
        d = d | u32(a[i] ^ b[i])
    }
    d == 0
}

impl<G: Game> Engine<G> {
    // ---- the host's side --------------------------------------------------------------------

    /// Starts a call.
    pub fn begin(mut self) {
        self.call += 1
    }

    /// Ends a call: the queue's work, then a refusal for each request whose work ended unanswered,
    /// so none waits for the host's timeout.
    pub fn end(mut self) {
        self.verify_some()
        var left: Vec<u32> = Vec::new()
        for c in self.conns {
            if c.asked && !c.answered && !self.busy(c.conn) {
                left.push(c.conn)
            }
        }
        for conn in left {
            self.refuse(conn, "The server couldn't do that just now. Try again in a moment.")
        }
    }

    /// Request `conn` opened.
    pub fn opened(mut self, conn: u32) {
        self.closed(conn)
        self.conns.push(
            Conn {
                conn,
                asked: false,
                answered: false,
                public: false,
                session: Vec::new(),
                account: 0,
                csrf: Vec::new(),
                fresh_until: 0,
                recovery: false,
                me: None,
                ceremony: Vec::new(),
                cookies: Vec::new(),
                pending: None,
            },
        )
    }

    /// Request `conn` closed (answered, or its client went): its jobs finish their writes, and an
    /// upload it waited for is verified all the same.
    pub fn closed(mut self, conn: u32) {
        var i = 0
        while i < self.conns.len() {
            if self.conns[i].conn == conn {
                let _ = self.conns.remove(i)
            } else {
                i += 1
            }
        }
        self.closed_upload(conn)
    }

    /// Request `conn`'s request: read its session from its cookie, if it has one, then do it.
    pub fn http(mut self, conn: u32, asked: Asked) {
        if self.conn_index(conn).is_none() {
            self.opened(conn)
        }
        let Some(i) = self.conn_index(conn) else { return }
        self.now = max(self.now, asked.time)
        self.conns[i].asked = true
        self.conns[i].public = asked.public
        self.conns[i].ceremony = asked.ceremony.clone()
        let request: Option<Request> = read(asked.body)
        let Some(request) = request else {
            self.refuse(conn, "That request isn't one we read.")
            return
        }
        let public = match request {
            Request::Board { .. } | Request::Watch { .. } => true,
            _ => false,
        }
        if asked.public && !public {
            self.refuse(conn, "That request changes things: it can't be a GET.")
            return
        }
        // The public reads and an upload (by a game's token) are no session's.
        let sessionless = public || match request {
            Request::Upload { .. } => true,
            _ => false,
        }
        if sessionless || asked.session.is_empty() {
            self.request(conn, request)
            return
        }
        if asked.session.len() != TOKEN_BYTES {
            self.session_gone(conn)
            self.request(conn, request)
            return
        }
        self.conns[i].pending = Some(request.clone())
        var job = blank_job(conn, Request::Me)
        job.hash = hashed(asked.session)
        let k = session_key(job.hash)
        self.get(take k, Step::HelloSession, take job)
    }

    /// The host's answer to ticket `ticket`: its bytes, or none if the request failed.
    pub fn answer(mut self, ticket: u32, answer: Option<Vec<u8>>) {
        if self.nudge == Some(ticket) {
            self.nudge = None
            return
        }
        if self.queue_scan == Some(ticket) {
            self.queue_scan = None
            self.queue_answered(answer)
            return
        }
        var found: Option<u32> = None
        for i in 0..self.jobs.len() {
            if self.jobs[i].ticket == ticket {
                found = Some(i)
            }
        }
        let Some(i) = found else { return }
        let job = self.jobs.remove(i)
        if job.step == Step::QueueAccount {
            self.queue_scan = None
        }
        match answer {
            Some(bytes) => self.advance(take job, bytes),
            None => self.refuse(
                job.conn,
                "The server couldn't do that just now. Try again in a moment.",
            ),
        }
    }

    /// What the server asks of its host, since the last time.
    pub fn commands(mut self) -> Vec<Command> {
        let out = self.out.clone()
        self.out.clear()
        out
    }

    /// The server's clock now, in milliseconds.
    pub fn clock_now(self) -> u64 {
        self.now
    }

    // ---- helpers ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    fn next_ticket(mut self) -> u32 {
        self.ticket += 1
        self.ticket
    }

    fn conn_index(self, conn: u32) -> Option<u32> {
        for i in 0..self.conns.len() {
            if self.conns[i].conn == conn {
                return Some(i)
            }
        }
        None
    }

    /// Whether request `conn` still has work under way: a job, its session being read, or an upload
    /// being verified.
    fn busy(self, conn: u32) -> bool {
        for j in self.jobs {
            if j.conn == conn {
                return true
            }
        }
        for (c, _) in self.uploads {
            if c == conn {
                return true
            }
        }
        false
    }

    /// Answers request `conn` with `reply`, once: a public read's answer may be cached.
    fn reply(mut self, conn: u32, reply: take Reply) {
        let Some(i) = self.conn_index(conn) else { return }
        if self.conns[i].answered {
            return
        }
        self.conns[i].answered = true
        let public = if !self.conns[i].public { 0 } else {
            match reply {
                Reply::Board { .. } => BOARD_AGE,
                Reply::Run { .. } => RUN_AGE,
                _ => 0,
            }
        }
        let cookies = self.conns[i].cookies.clone()
        self.out.push(Command::Respond { conn, body: save(reply), cookies, public })
    }

    fn refuse(mut self, conn: u32, why: Text) {
        self.reply(conn, Reply::Refused { why: String::from(why) })
    }

    /// Answers request `conn` with its session's account (or nobody) and CSRF token.
    fn welcome(mut self, conn: u32) {
        let (me, csrf) = match self.conn_index(conn) {
            Some(i) => (self.conns[i].me.clone().unwrap_or(nobody()), self.conns[i].csrf.clone()),
            None => (nobody(), Vec::new()),
        }
        self.reply(conn, Reply::Welcome { me, csrf })
    }

    /// Request `conn`'s account is now `me`.
    fn set_me(mut self, conn: u32, me: take Me) {
        if let Some(i) = self.conn_index(conn) {
            self.conns[i].me = Some(take me)
        }
    }

    /// Answers the request that waits for run `run`, if one still does.
    fn tell(mut self, run: u64, reply: take Reply) {
        var waiting: Option<u32> = None
        for (c, r) in self.uploads {
            if r == run {
                waiting = Some(c)
            }
        }
        let Some(conn) = waiting else { return }
        self.closed_upload(conn)
        self.reply(conn, take reply)
    }

    fn closed_upload(mut self, conn: u32) {
        var i = 0
        while i < self.uploads.len() {
            if self.uploads[i].0 == conn {
                let _ = self.uploads.remove(i)
            } else {
                i += 1
            }
        }
    }

    /// Sets cookie `name` on request `conn`'s response (`value` empty and `max_age` 0 clear it).
    fn cookie(mut self, conn: u32, name: Text, value: take Vec<u8>, max_age: u32) {
        let Some(i) = self.conn_index(conn) else { return }
        self.conns[i].cookies.push(Cookie { name: String::from(name), value, max_age })
    }

    /// Request `conn`'s session cookie is for no session (any more): it is cleared.
    fn session_gone(mut self, conn: u32) {
        self.cookie(conn, SESSION, Vec::new(), 0)
    }

    /// Request `conn`'s session is read: its request goes on.
    fn hello_done(mut self, conn: u32) {
        let Some(i) = self.conn_index(conn) else { return }
        let pending = replace(mut self.conns[i].pending, None)
        if let Some(r) = pending {
            self.request(conn, r)
        }
    }

    fn get(mut self, key: take Vec<u8>, step: Step, job: take Job) {
        var j = take job
        let t = self.next_ticket()
        self.out.push(Command::Get { ticket: t, key })
        j.ticket = t
        j.step = step
        self.jobs.push(take j)
    }

    fn scan(mut self, from: take Vec<u8>, limit: u32, step: Step, job: take Job) {
        let to = past(from).unwrap_or(Vec::new())
        self.scan_range(take from, take to, limit, step, take job)
    }

    fn scan_range(
        mut self,
        from: take Vec<u8>,
        to: take Vec<u8>,
        limit: u32,
        step: Step,
        job: take Job,
    ) {
        var j = take job
        let t = self.next_ticket()
        self.out.push(Command::Scan { ticket: t, from, to, limit, down: false })
        j.ticket = t
        j.step = step
        self.jobs.push(take j)
    }

    fn random(mut self, n: u32, step: Step, job: take Job) {
        var j = take job
        let t = self.next_ticket()
        self.out.push(Command::Random { ticket: t, n })
        j.ticket = t
        j.step = step
        self.jobs.push(take j)
    }

    fn put<T: Serialize>(mut self, key: take Vec<u8>, record: T) {
        self.out.push(Command::Put { key, value: save(record) })
    }

    fn put_bytes(mut self, key: take Vec<u8>, value: take Vec<u8>) {
        self.out.push(Command::Put { key, value })
    }

    fn delete(mut self, key: take Vec<u8>) {
        self.out.push(Command::Delete { key })
    }

    /// The request's account, if it is signed in with a session whose CSRF token is `csrf`
    /// (none: no token asked for), and a passkey session unless `recovery` allows one made by a
    /// code; a refusal said if not.
    fn signed_in(mut self, conn: u32, csrf: Option<Vec<u8>>, recovery: bool) -> Option<Conn> {
        let Some(i) = self.conn_index(conn) else { return None }
        let c = self.conns[i].clone()
        if c.session.is_empty() {
            self.refuse(conn, "Sign in first.")
            return None
        }
        if let Some(token) = csrf {
            if !same_bytes(token, c.csrf) {
                self.refuse(conn, "That request didn't come from this console. Reload it.")
                return None
            }
        }
        if c.recovery && !recovery {
            self.refuse(conn, "Add a passkey first: you signed in with a recovery code.")
            return None
        }
        Some(c)
    }

    /// Like `signed_in`, and the sign-in fresh: within `FRESH` of a passkey's, or by a code.
    fn fresh(mut self, conn: u32, csrf: Vec<u8>, recovery: bool) -> Option<Conn> {
        let c = self.signed_in(conn, Some(csrf.clone()), recovery)?
        if !c.recovery && c.fresh_until < self.now {
            self.refuse(
                conn,
                "Sign in with your passkey again first: this needs a fresh sign-in.",
            )
            return None
        }
        Some(c)
    }

    /// Takes the ceremony of `kind` that request `conn`'s cookie names, then goes on with `job`
    /// (`CeremonyTaken`); refused if it has none, or one that has expired or was used. It is used up
    /// whatever comes of it: deleted, and its cookie cleared.
    fn take_ceremony(mut self, conn: u32, kind: u32, job: take Job) {
        var j = take job
        let Some(i) = self.conn_index(conn) else { return }
        let v = self.conns[i].ceremony.clone()
        if v.len() != 8 + CEREMONY_BYTES {
            self.refuse(conn, expired(kind))
            return
        }
        let expires = u64_at(v, 0)
        let key = ceremony_key(expires, hashed(part(v, 8, CEREMONY_BYTES)))
        self.cookie(conn, CEREMONY, Vec::new(), 0)
        if expires < self.now || lately(self.spent, key) {
            self.refuse(conn, expired(kind))
            return
        }
        // Used now: a read made before this call's delete commits would still find it.
        remember(mut self.spent, key.clone())
        self.delete(key.clone())
        j.n = kind
        self.get(take key, Step::CeremonyTaken, take j)
    }

    fn is_signed_in(self, conn: u32) -> bool {
        match self.conn_index(conn) {
            Some(i) => !self.conns[i].session.is_empty(),
            None => false,
        }
    }

    fn expected(self, challenge: Vec<u8>) -> Expected {
        Expected {
            rp_id: self.rp_id.clone(),
            origin: self.origin.clone(),
            challenge: challenge.clone(),
        }
    }

    /// Binds connection `conn` to a session.
    fn bind(mut self, conn: u32, hash: Vec<u8>, s: Session) {
        if let Some(i) = self.conn_index(conn) {
            self.conns[i].session = hash.clone()
            self.conns[i].account = s.account
            self.conns[i].csrf = s.csrf.clone()
            self.conns[i].fresh_until = s.fresh_until
            self.conns[i].recovery = s.recovery
        }
    }

    /// Lets go of every request's binding to the session `hash` (every session, if empty) of
    /// `account`: a request under way of a session that ended is no longer signed in.
    fn unbind(mut self, account: u64, hash: Vec<u8>) {
        for i in 0..self.conns.len() {
            let c = self.conns[i].clone()
            if c.account == account &&
                !c.session.is_empty() &&
                (hash.is_empty() || same_bytes(c.session, hash)) {
                self.conns[i].session = Vec::new()
                self.conns[i].account = 0
                self.conns[i].csrf = Vec::new()
                self.conns[i].recovery = false
                self.conns[i].me = None
            }
        }
    }

    /// Writes a new session for `account` from `secrets` (its token, then its CSRF token), binds
    /// request `conn` to it, sets its cookie, and answers with it.
    fn begin_session(
        mut self,
        conn: u32,
        a: Account,
        secrets: [u8],
        recovery: bool,
        codes: Vec<String>,
    ) {
        let token = part(secrets, 0, TOKEN_BYTES)
        let csrf = part(secrets, TOKEN_BYTES, CSRF_BYTES)
        let hash = hashed(token)
        let s = Session {
            account: a.id,
            csrf: csrf.clone(),
            created: self.now,
            seen: self.now,
            fresh_until: self.now + FRESH,
            recovery,
        }
        self.put(session_key(hash), s.clone())
        self.put(
            indexed(a.id, OF_SESSION, hash),
            SessionView { id: public_id(hash), created: self.now, seen: self.now, this: false },
        )
        self.bind(conn, hash.clone(), s.clone())
        self.cookie(conn, SESSION, take token, u32(SESSION_LIFE / 1000))
        self.reply(conn, Reply::Session { csrf, me: me_of(a, recovery), codes: codes.clone() })
    }

    /// Writes recovery codes for account `id` from `bytes`, and gives them as text.
    fn write_codes(mut self, id: u64, bytes: [u8]) -> Vec<String> {
        var codes: Vec<String> = Vec::new()
        for k in 0..CODES {
            let c = code(part(bytes, k * CODE_BYTES, CODE_BYTES))
            let Some(h) = code_hash(c.as_str()) else { panic("a code reads back") }
            self.put(code_key(h), Recovery { account: id })
            self.put_bytes(indexed(id, OF_CODE, h), Vec::new())
            codes.push(take c)
        }
        codes
    }

    // ---- requests -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

    fn request(mut self, conn: u32, request: Request) {
        var job = blank_job(conn, request.clone())
        match request {
            // The session was read from its cookie (`http`): this is what it found.
            Request::Me => self.welcome(conn),
            Request::Begin { ceremony, csrf } => {
                if ceremony == REGISTER && self.is_signed_in(conn) {
                    self.refuse(conn, "Sign out first to make another account.")
                    return
                }
                if ceremony == REGISTER || ceremony == SIGN_IN {
                    // The challenge and the browser's token; a new account's handle, number and
                    // name come with them.
                    job.n = ceremony
                    let n = if ceremony == REGISTER {
                        CHALLENGE_BYTES + CEREMONY_BYTES + HANDLE_BYTES + 16
                    } else { CHALLENGE_BYTES + CEREMONY_BYTES }
                    self.random(n, Step::BeginRandom, take job)
                } else if ceremony == ADD_PASSKEY {
                    let Some(c) = self.fresh(conn, csrf, recovery: true) else { return }
                    job.n = ceremony
                    job.id = c.account
                    self.scan(
                        indexed(c.account, OF_PASSKEY, []),
                        MOST_PASSKEYS,
                        Step::BeginAddScan,
                        take job,
                    )
                } else {
                    self.refuse(conn, "That isn't a ceremony.")
                }
            },
            Request::Register { .. } | Request::SignIn { .. } => {
                let kind = match request {
                    Request::Register { .. } => REGISTER,
                    _ => SIGN_IN,
                }
                self.take_ceremony(conn, kind, take job)
            },
            Request::Recover { code } => {
                recent(mut self.tries, self.now, MINUTE)
                if self.tries.len() >= ALL_TRIES {
                    self.refuse(conn, "Too many tries. Wait a few minutes, then try again.")
                    return
                }
                self.tries.push(self.now)
                let Some(h) = code_hash(code.as_str()) else {
                    self.refuse(
                        conn,
                        "That isn't a recovery code: it has 16 letters and digits.",
                    )
                    return
                }
                job.hash = h.clone()
                self.get(code_key(h), Step::RecoverCode, take job)
            },
            Request::Reroll { csrf } => {
                let Some(c) = self.signed_in(conn, Some(csrf.clone()), recovery: false) else {
                    return
                }
                self.get(account_key(c.account), Step::NameAccount, take job)
            },
            Request::Keep { csrf } => {
                let Some(c) = self.signed_in(conn, Some(csrf.clone()), recovery: false) else {
                    return
                }
                self.get(account_key(c.account), Step::NameAccount, take job)
            },
            Request::AddPasskey { csrf, .. } => {
                let Some(c) = self.fresh(conn, csrf, recovery: true) else { return }
                job.id = c.account
                job.hash = c.session.clone()
                self.take_ceremony(conn, ADD_PASSKEY, take job)
            },
            Request::RemovePasskey { csrf, id } => {
                let Some(c) = self.fresh(conn, csrf, recovery: false) else { return }
                job.id = c.account
                job.message = id.clone()
                self.scan(
                    indexed(c.account, OF_PASSKEY, []),
                    MOST_PASSKEYS + 1,
                    Step::RemoveScan,
                    take job,
                )
            },
            Request::Passkeys => {
                let Some(c) = self.signed_in(conn, None, recovery: true) else { return }
                self.scan(
                    indexed(c.account, OF_PASSKEY, []),
                    MOST_PASSKEYS + 1,
                    Step::PasskeysScan,
                    take job,
                )
            },
            Request::NewCodes { csrf } => {
                let Some(c) = self.fresh(conn, csrf, recovery: false) else { return }
                job.id = c.account
                self.scan(indexed(c.account, OF_CODE, []), 4 * CODES, Step::CodesScan, take job)
            },
            Request::Sessions => {
                let Some(c) = self.signed_in(conn, None, recovery: true) else { return }
                job.id = c.account
                job.hash = c.session.clone()
                self.scan(indexed(c.account, OF_SESSION, []), 256, Step::SessionsScan, take job)
            },
            Request::Revoke { csrf, session } => {
                let Some(c) = self.signed_in(conn, Some(csrf.clone()), recovery: true) else {
                    return
                }
                job.id = c.account
                job.hash = c.session.clone()
                job.message = session.clone()
                self.scan(indexed(c.account, OF_SESSION, []), 256, Step::RevokeScan, take job)
            },
            Request::SignOut { csrf } => {
                let Some(c) = self.signed_in(conn, Some(csrf.clone()), recovery: true) else {
                    return
                }
                self.delete(session_key(c.session))
                self.delete(indexed(c.account, OF_SESSION, c.session))
                self.unbind(c.account, c.session.clone())
                self.session_gone(conn)
                self.welcome(conn)
            },
            Request::Token { game } => {
                let Some(c) = self.signed_in(conn, None, recovery: false) else { return }
                if game.as_str() != self.game.id() {
                    self.refuse(conn, "That game has no boards here.")
                    return
                }
                self.get(account_key(c.account), Step::TokenAccount, take job)
            },
            Request::Export { part } => {
                let Some(c) = self.signed_in(conn, None, recovery: true) else { return }
                job.id = c.account
                job.category = part
                self.get(account_key(c.account), Step::ExportAccount, take job)
            },
            Request::Delete { csrf } => {
                let Some(c) = self.fresh(conn, csrf, recovery: false) else { return }
                job.id = c.account
                self.get(account_key(c.account), Step::DeleteAccount, take job)
            },
            Request::Upload { token, game, replay } => {
                if game.as_str() != self.game.id() {
                    self.reply(
                        conn,
                        Reply::Rejected { why: String::from("That game has no boards here.") },
                    )
                    return
                }
                if replay.len() > MOST_REPLAY || token.len() != TOKEN_BYTES {
                    self.reply(
                        conn,
                        Reply::Rejected { why: String::from("That run is too long to upload.") },
                    )
                    return
                }
                match self.game.claim(replay) {
                    Ok(claim) => {
                        job.category = claim.course
                        job.tries = claim.ticks
                        job.message = replay.clone()
                        self.get(token_key(hashed(token)), Step::UploadToken, take job)
                    },
                    Err(why) => self.reply(conn, Reply::Rejected { why: String::from(why) }),
                }
            },
            Request::Board { game, course, category, from } => {
                if game.as_str() != self.game.id() ||
                    (course >= self.game.courses() && course != WHOLE) ||
                    (category != ANY && category != FULL) ||
                    from > 10000 {
                    self.refuse(conn, "There's no such board.")
                    return
                }
                job.n = from
                let prefix = if course == WHOLE {
                    whole_prefix(game, self.game.board(), category)
                } else { board_prefix(game, self.game.board(), course, category) }
                self.scan(take prefix, from + BOARD_PAGE + 1, Step::BoardScan, take job)
            },
            Request::Watch { run } => {
                self.get(run_key(run), Step::WatchRun, take job)
            },
        }
    }

    // ---- answers ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    fn advance(mut self, job: take Job, answer: Vec<u8>) {
        var j = take job
        let conn = j.conn
        match j.step {
            Step::HelloSession => {
                let s: Option<Session> = got(answer)
                let Some(s) = s else {
                    self.session_gone(conn)
                    self.hello_done(conn)
                    return
                }
                if s.created + SESSION_LIFE < self.now {
                    self.delete(session_key(j.hash))
                    self.delete(indexed(s.account, OF_SESSION, j.hash))
                    self.session_gone(conn)
                    self.hello_done(conn)
                    return
                }
                j.session = Some(s.clone())
                self.get(account_key(s.account), Step::HelloAccount, take j)
            },
            Step::HelloAccount => {
                let a: Option<Account> = got(answer)
                let Some(s) = j.session.clone() else { return }
                let Some(a) = a else {
                    self.session_gone(conn)
                    self.hello_done(conn)
                    return
                }
                if a.deleting {
                    self.session_gone(conn)
                    self.hello_done(conn)
                    return
                }
                var seen = s.clone()
                seen.seen = self.now
                // A session resumed when the console starts is no longer fresh: freshness is a
                // sign-in's. It is written then, or when it was last seen an hour ago, not with
                // every request.
                let resumed = match self.conn_index(conn) {
                    Some(i) => match self.conns[i].pending {
                        Some(Request::Me) => true,
                        _ => false,
                    },
                    None => false,
                }
                if resumed {
                    seen.fresh_until = 0
                }
                if resumed || s.seen + HOUR < self.now {
                    self.put(session_key(j.hash), seen.clone())
                    self.put(
                        indexed(a.id, OF_SESSION, j.hash),
                        SessionView {
                            id: public_id(j.hash),
                            created: s.created,
                            seen: self.now,
                            this: false,
                        },
                    )
                }
                self.bind(conn, j.hash.clone(), seen.clone())
                if let Some(i) = self.conn_index(conn) {
                    self.conns[i].me = Some(me_of(a, s.recovery))
                }
                self.hello_done(conn)
            },
            Step::BeginRandom => {
                if answer.len() < CHALLENGE_BYTES + CEREMONY_BYTES {
                    self.refuse(conn, "The server couldn't start that. Try again.")
                    return
                }
                let challenge = part(answer, 0, CHALLENGE_BYTES)
                let token = part(answer, CHALLENGE_BYTES, CEREMONY_BYTES)
                let at = CHALLENGE_BYTES + CEREMONY_BYTES
                var c = Ceremony {
                    kind: j.n,
                    challenge: challenge.clone(),
                    handle: Vec::new(),
                    account: 0,
                    seed: 0,
                    expires: self.now + CHALLENGE_LIFE,
                }
                if j.n == ADD_PASSKEY {
                    c.handle = j.hash.clone()
                    c.account = j.id
                }
                if j.n == REGISTER {
                    if answer.len() < at + HANDLE_BYTES + 16 {
                        self.refuse(conn, "The server couldn't start that. Try again.")
                        return
                    }
                    c.handle = part(answer, at, HANDLE_BYTES)
                    c.account = u64_at(answer, at + HANDLE_BYTES)
                    c.seed = u64_at(answer, at + HANDLE_BYTES + 8)
                }
                let handle = c.handle.clone()
                // Kept under the token's hash; the browser keeps the token, and when it expires.
                var held: Vec<u8> = Vec::new()
                append_u64(mut held, c.expires)
                for b in token {
                    held.push(b)
                }
                self.put(ceremony_key(c.expires, hashed(token)), c.clone())
                self.cookie(conn, CEREMONY, take held, u32(CHALLENGE_LIFE / 1000))
                self.reply(
                    conn,
                    Reply::Challenge { ceremony: j.n, challenge, handle, exclude: j.keys.clone() },
                )
                // Ceremonies begun and never finished go once they expire, a few as each begins.
                var to = ceremonies()
                append_u64(mut to, self.now)
                self.scan_range(ceremonies(), take to, PRUNED, Step::BeginPrune, take j)
            },
            Step::BeginPrune => {
                let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
                for e in es {
                    self.delete(e.key.clone())
                }
            },
            Step::CeremonyTaken => {
                let c: Option<Ceremony> = got(answer)
                let Some(c) = c else {
                    self.refuse(conn, expired(j.n))
                    return
                }
                if c.kind != j.n || c.expires < self.now {
                    self.refuse(conn, expired(j.n))
                    return
                }
                match j.request.clone() {
                    Request::Register { id, client_data, attestation } => {
                        match registration(
                            id,
                            client_data,
                            attestation,
                            self.expected(c.challenge.clone()),
                        ) {
                            Ok(cred) => {
                                j.credential = Some(cred.clone())
                                j.id = c.account
                                j.seed = c.seed
                                j.hash = c.handle.clone()
                                self.get(passkey_key(cred.id), Step::RegisterCredential, take j)
                            },
                            Err(why) => self.refuse(conn, why),
                        }
                    },
                    Request::SignIn { id, .. } => {
                        j.message = c.challenge.clone()
                        self.get(passkey_key(id), Step::SignInCredential, take j)
                    },
                    Request::AddPasskey { id, client_data, attestation, .. } => {
                        // Begun by this account, in a session of its.
                        if c.account != j.id {
                            self.refuse(conn, expired(j.n))
                            return
                        }
                        match registration(
                            id,
                            client_data,
                            attestation,
                            self.expected(c.challenge.clone()),
                        ) {
                            Ok(cred) => {
                                j.credential = Some(cred.clone())
                                self.get(passkey_key(cred.id), Step::AddCredential, take j)
                            },
                            Err(why) => self.refuse(conn, why),
                        }
                    },
                    _ => {},
                }
            },
            Step::BeginAddScan => {
                let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
                var exclude: Vec<Vec<u8>> = Vec::new()
                let skip = indexed(j.id, OF_PASSKEY, []).len()
                for e in es {
                    exclude.push(part(e.key, skip, e.key.len() - skip))
                }
                j.keys = take exclude
                self.get(account_key(j.id), Step::BeginAddAccount, take j)
            },
            Step::BeginAddAccount => {
                // A passkey added is made for the account's handle, as its first was.
                let a: Option<Account> = got(answer)
                let Some(a) = a else { return }
                j.hash = a.handle.clone()
                self.random(CHALLENGE_BYTES + CEREMONY_BYTES, Step::BeginRandom, take j)
            },
            Step::RegisterCredential => {
                if value(answer).is_some() {
                    self.refuse(conn, "That passkey is already an account's. Sign in with it.")
                    return
                }
                self.get(account_key(j.id), Step::RegisterAccount, take j)
            },
            Step::RegisterAccount => {
                if value(answer).is_some() || j.id == 0 {
                    self.refuse(conn, "The server couldn't make your account. Try again.")
                    return
                }
                let n = draw(j.seed)
                self.get(name_key(n), Step::RegisterName, take j)
            },
            Step::RegisterName | Step::NameTaken => {
                let n = draw(j.seed)
                if value(answer).is_some() || lately(self.recent_names, name_key(n)) {
                    // Taken: another draw, a few times.
                    j.tries += 1
                    if j.tries > 8 {
                        self.refuse(conn, "The server couldn't find a name. Try again.")
                        return
                    }
                    let next = if j.step == Step::RegisterName { Step::RegisterSeed } else {
                        Step::NameSeed
                    }
                    self.random(8, next, take j)
                    return
                }
                if j.step == Step::RegisterName {
                    j.account = Some(
                        Account {
                            id: j.id,
                            handle: j.hash.clone(),
                            name: n,
                            fixed: false,
                            rerolls: REROLLS,
                            created: self.now,
                            deleting: false,
                        },
                    )
                    self.random(
                        TOKEN_BYTES + CSRF_BYTES + CODES * CODE_BYTES,
                        Step::RegisterSecrets,
                        take j,
                    )
                } else {
                    self.renamed(take j, n)
                }
            },
            Step::RegisterSeed | Step::NameSeed => {
                if answer.len() < 8 {
                    return
                }
                j.seed = u64_at(answer, 0)
                let next = if j.step == Step::RegisterSeed { Step::RegisterName } else {
                    Step::NameTaken
                }
                self.get(name_key(draw(j.seed)), next, take j)
            },
            Step::RegisterSecrets => {
                let Some(a) = j.account.clone() else { return }
                let Some(cred) = j.credential.clone() else { return }
                if answer.len() < TOKEN_BYTES + CSRF_BYTES + CODES * CODE_BYTES {
                    return
                }
                self.put(account_key(a.id), a.clone())
                self.put_bytes(name_key(a.name), save(a.id))
                remember(mut self.recent_names, name_key(a.name))
                self.put(
                    passkey_key(cred.id),
                    Passkey {
                        account: a.id,
                        credential: cred.clone(),
                        created: self.now,
                        used: self.now,
                    },
                )
                self.put(
                    indexed(a.id, OF_PASSKEY, cred.id),
                    PasskeyView { id: cred.id.clone(), created: self.now, used: self.now },
                )
                let codes = self.write_codes(
                    a.id,
                    part(answer, TOKEN_BYTES + CSRF_BYTES, CODES * CODE_BYTES),
                )
                self.begin_session(conn, a, answer, recovery: false, codes: codes)
            },
            Step::SignInCredential => {
                let p: Option<Passkey> = got(answer)
                let Some(p) = p else {
                    self.refuse(
                        conn,
                        "That passkey isn't one we know. Its account may have been deleted.",
                    )
                    return
                }
                j.passkey = Some(p.clone())
                self.get(account_key(p.account), Step::SignInAccount, take j)
            },
            Step::SignInAccount => {
                let a: Option<Account> = got(answer)
                let Some(a) = a else {
                    self.refuse(conn, "That passkey's account is gone.")
                    return
                }
                let Some(p) = j.passkey.clone() else { return }
                let Request::SignIn {
                    client_data,
                    authenticator_data,
                    signature,
                    user,
                    ..
                } = j.request.clone() else {
                    return
                }
                if a.deleting || p.account != a.id {
                    self.refuse(conn, "That passkey's account is gone.")
                    return
                }
                // The browser names the account the passkey was made for: it must be this one.
                if !user.is_empty() && !same_bytes(user, a.handle) {
                    self.refuse(conn, "That passkey belongs to another account.")
                    return
                }
                match assertion(
                    client_data,
                    authenticator_data,
                    self.expected(j.message.clone()),
                    p.credential.clone(),
                ) {
                    Ok(signed) => {
                        j.account = Some(a.clone())
                        j.n = signed.counter
                        let t = self.next_ticket()
                        self.out.push(
                            Command::Verify {
                                ticket: t,
                                algorithm: p.credential.signature(),
                                key: p.credential.key.clone(),
                                message: signed.message.clone(),
                                signature,
                            },
                        )
                        j.ticket = t
                        j.step = Step::SignInVerify
                        self.jobs.push(take j)
                    },
                    Err(why) => self.refuse(conn, why),
                }
            },
            Step::SignInVerify => {
                if !verified(answer) {
                    self.refuse(conn, "That passkey's signature doesn't check out.")
                    return
                }
                self.random(TOKEN_BYTES + CSRF_BYTES, Step::SignInSecrets, take j)
            },
            Step::SignInSecrets => {
                let Some(a) = j.account.clone() else { return }
                let Some(p) = j.passkey.clone() else { return }
                if answer.len() < TOKEN_BYTES + CSRF_BYTES {
                    return
                }
                var used = p.clone()
                used.credential.counter = j.n
                used.used = self.now
                self.put(passkey_key(p.credential.id), used.clone())
                self.put(
                    indexed(a.id, OF_PASSKEY, p.credential.id),
                    PasskeyView { id: p.credential.id.clone(), created: p.created, used: self.now },
                )
                self.begin_session(conn, a, answer, recovery: false, codes: Vec::new())
            },
            Step::RecoverCode => {
                let r: Option<Recovery> = got(answer)
                let Some(r) = r else {
                    self.refuse(conn, "That code isn't one we know, or it has been used.")
                    return
                }
                j.id = r.account
                self.get(account_key(r.account), Step::RecoverAccount, take j)
            },
            Step::RecoverAccount => {
                let a: Option<Account> = got(answer)
                let Some(a) = a else {
                    self.refuse(conn, "That code's account is gone.")
                    return
                }
                if a.deleting {
                    self.refuse(conn, "That code's account is gone.")
                    return
                }
                // Used up, and every other session ends.
                self.delete(code_key(j.hash))
                self.delete(indexed(a.id, OF_CODE, j.hash))
                j.account = Some(a.clone())
                self.scan(indexed(a.id, OF_SESSION, []), 256, Step::RecoverSessions, take j)
            },
            Step::RecoverSessions => {
                let Some(a) = j.account.clone() else { return }
                let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
                let skip = indexed(a.id, OF_SESSION, []).len()
                for e in es {
                    let h = part(e.key, skip, e.key.len() - skip)
                    self.delete(session_key(h))
                    self.delete(e.key.clone())
                }
                self.unbind(a.id, Vec::new())
                self.random(TOKEN_BYTES + CSRF_BYTES, Step::RecoverSecrets, take j)
            },
            Step::RecoverSecrets => {
                let Some(a) = j.account.clone() else { return }
                if answer.len() < TOKEN_BYTES + CSRF_BYTES {
                    return
                }
                self.begin_session(conn, a, answer, recovery: true, codes: Vec::new())
            },
            Step::NameAccount => {
                let a: Option<Account> = got(answer)
                let Some(a) = a else { return }
                if a.fixed {
                    self.refuse(conn, "Your name is fixed.")
                    return
                }
                match j.request {
                    Request::Keep { .. } => {
                        var kept = a.clone()
                        kept.fixed = true
                        self.put(account_key(a.id), kept.clone())
                        self.set_me(conn, me_of(kept, recovery: false))
                        self.welcome(conn)
                    },
                    _ => {
                        if a.rerolls == 0 {
                            self.refuse(conn, "There are no draws left.")
                            return
                        }
                        j.account = Some(a.clone())
                        self.random(8, Step::NameSeed, take j)
                    },
                }
            },
            Step::AddCredential => {
                if value(answer).is_some() {
                    self.refuse(conn, "That passkey is already an account's.")
                    return
                }
                self.scan(indexed(j.id, OF_PASSKEY, []), MOST_PASSKEYS + 1, Step::AddCount, take j)
            },
            Step::AddCount => {
                let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
                if es.len() >= MOST_PASSKEYS {
                    self.refuse(
                        conn,
                        "An account has at most 16 passkeys. Remove one first.",
                    )
                    return
                }
                let Some(cred) = j.credential.clone() else { return }
                self.put(
                    passkey_key(cred.id),
                    Passkey { account: j.id, credential: cred.clone(), created: self.now, used: 0 },
                )
                self.put(
                    indexed(j.id, OF_PASSKEY, cred.id),
                    PasskeyView { id: cred.id.clone(), created: self.now, used: 0 },
                )
                self.get(session_key(j.hash), Step::AddSession, take j)
            },
            Step::AddSession => {
                // A session a code made is a whole one once it has added a passkey.
                let s: Option<Session> = got(answer)
                if let Some(s) = s {
                    if s.recovery {
                        var whole = s.clone()
                        whole.recovery = false
                        whole.fresh_until = self.now + FRESH
                        self.put(session_key(j.hash), whole.clone())
                        self.bind(conn, j.hash.clone(), whole.clone())
                    }
                }
                self.get(account_key(j.id), Step::TokenAccount, take j)
                // TokenAccount with no game asked answers with the account, below.
            },
            Step::RemoveScan => {
                let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
                let skip = indexed(j.id, OF_PASSKEY, []).len()
                var found = false
                var left: Vec<PasskeyView> = Vec::new()
                for e in es {
                    let id = part(e.key, skip, e.key.len() - skip)
                    if same_bytes(id, j.message) {
                        found = true
                    } else if let Some(v) = read::<PasskeyView>(e.value) {
                        left.push(take v)
                    }
                }
                if !found {
                    self.refuse(conn, "That passkey isn't one of yours.")
                    return
                }
                if left.is_empty() {
                    self.refuse(
                        conn,
                        "That's your only passkey: add another before you remove it.",
                    )
                    return
                }
                self.delete(passkey_key(j.message))
                self.delete(indexed(j.id, OF_PASSKEY, j.message))
                self.reply(conn, Reply::Passkeys { passkeys: left })
            },
            Step::PasskeysScan => {
                let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
                var list: Vec<PasskeyView> = Vec::new()
                for e in es {
                    if let Some(v) = read::<PasskeyView>(e.value) {
                        list.push(take v)
                    }
                }
                self.reply(conn, Reply::Passkeys { passkeys: list })
            },
            Step::CodesScan => {
                let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
                let skip = indexed(j.id, OF_CODE, []).len()
                for e in es {
                    self.delete(code_key(part(e.key, skip, e.key.len() - skip)))
                    self.delete(e.key.clone())
                }
                self.random(CODES * CODE_BYTES, Step::CodesRandom, take j)
            },
            Step::CodesRandom => {
                if answer.len() < CODES * CODE_BYTES {
                    return
                }
                let codes = self.write_codes(j.id, answer)
                self.reply(conn, Reply::Codes { codes })
            },
            Step::SessionsScan | Step::RevokeScan => {
                let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
                let skip = indexed(j.id, OF_SESSION, []).len()
                var list: Vec<SessionView> = Vec::new()
                var revoked = false
                for e in es {
                    let h = part(e.key, skip, e.key.len() - skip)
                    let Some(v) = read::<SessionView>(e.value) else { continue }
                    if j.step == Step::RevokeScan && same_bytes(public_id(h), j.message) {
                        self.delete(session_key(h))
                        self.delete(e.key.clone())
                        self.unbind(j.id, h.clone())
                        revoked = true
                        continue
                    }
                    var view = v.clone()
                    view.this = same_bytes(h, j.hash)
                    list.push(take view)
                }
                if j.step == Step::RevokeScan && !revoked {
                    self.refuse(conn, "That session has already ended.")
                    return
                }
                if j.step == Step::RevokeScan && !self.is_signed_in(conn) {
                    // This session itself.
                    self.session_gone(conn)
                    self.welcome(conn)
                    return
                }
                self.reply(conn, Reply::Sessions { sessions: list })
            },
            Step::TokenAccount => {
                let a: Option<Account> = got(answer)
                let Some(a) = a else { return }
                match j.request {
                    Request::Token { .. } => {
                        if !a.fixed {
                            self.refuse(conn, "Be knighted first: keep your name.")
                            return
                        }
                        j.account = Some(a.clone())
                        self.scan(indexed(a.id, OF_TOKEN, []), 64, Step::TokenPrune, take j)
                    },
                    // A passkey added: the account as it is now.
                    _ => {
                        if let Some(i) = self.conn_index(conn) {
                            self.conns[i].me = Some(me_of(a, self.conns[i].recovery))
                        }
                        self.welcome(conn)
                    },
                }
            },
            Step::TokenPrune => {
                // Tokens that have expired go as a new one comes.
                let Some(a) = j.account.clone() else { return }
                let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
                let skip = indexed(a.id, OF_TOKEN, []).len()
                for e in es {
                    if e.value.len() == 8 && u64_at(e.value, 0) < self.now {
                        self.delete(token_key(part(e.key, skip, e.key.len() - skip)))
                        self.delete(e.key.clone())
                    }
                }
                self.random(TOKEN_BYTES, Step::TokenRandom, take j)
            },
            Step::TokenRandom => {
                let Some(a) = j.account.clone() else { return }
                if answer.len() < TOKEN_BYTES {
                    return
                }
                let token = part(answer, 0, TOKEN_BYTES)
                var expires: Vec<u8> = Vec::new()
                append_u64(mut expires, self.now + TOKEN_LIFE)
                self.put_bytes(indexed(a.id, OF_TOKEN, hashed(token)), take expires)
                self.put(
                    token_key(hashed(token)),
                    GameToken {
                        account: a.id,
                        game: String::from(self.game.id()),
                        expires: self.now + TOKEN_LIFE,
                    },
                )
                self.reply(conn, Reply::Token { token, expires_in: u32(TOKEN_LIFE / 1000) })
            },
            Step::ExportAccount => {
                let a: Option<Account> = got(answer)
                let Some(a) = a else { return }
                j.text = export_head(a)
                j.keys.clear()
                self.scan(under_account(j.id), 512, Step::ExportScan, take j)
            },
            Step::ExportScan => {
                let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
                let prefix = under_account(j.id)
                for e in es {
                    if e.key.len() <= prefix.len() {
                        continue
                    }
                    let of = e.key[prefix.len()]
                    let rest = part(e.key, prefix.len() + 1, e.key.len() - prefix.len() - 1)
                    export_entry(mut j.text, of, rest, e.value)
                    if of == OF_RUN && rest.len() == 8 {
                        j.keys.push(run_key(u64_at(rest, 0)))
                    }
                    if self.export_flush(mut j, last: false) {
                        return
                    }
                }
                if es.len() == 512 {
                    borrow last = es[es.len() - 1].key
                    var from = last.clone()
                    from.push(0)
                    let to = past(prefix).unwrap_or(Vec::new())
                    self.scan_range(take from, take to, 512, Step::ExportScan, take j)
                    return
                }
                j.text.push_str("],\"replays\":[")
                self.export_next_run(take j)
            },
            Step::ExportRun => {
                let r: Option<Run> = got(answer)
                if let Some(r) = r {
                    if j.n > 0 {
                        j.text.push_str(",")
                    }
                    j.n += 1
                    j.text.push_str(f"{{\"run\":\"{r.id}\",\"replay\":\"{base64url(r.replay)}\"}}")
                    if self.export_flush(mut j, last: false) {
                        return
                    }
                }
                self.export_next_run(take j)
            },
            Step::DeleteAccount => {
                let a: Option<Account> = got(answer)
                let Some(a) = a else { return }
                var going = a.clone()
                going.deleting = true
                self.put(account_key(a.id), going.clone())
                j.account = Some(take going)
                self.unbind(a.id, Vec::new())
                self.scan(under_account(a.id), 256, Step::DeleteScan, take j)
            },
            Step::DeleteNext => {
                let Some(a) = j.account.clone() else { return }
                self.scan(under_account(a.id), 256, Step::DeleteScan, take j)
            },
            Step::DeleteScan => {
                let Some(a) = j.account.clone() else { return }
                let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
                let prefix = under_account(a.id)
                for e in es {
                    if e.key.len() <= prefix.len() {
                        continue
                    }
                    let of = e.key[prefix.len()]
                    let rest = part(e.key, prefix.len() + 1, e.key.len() - prefix.len() - 1)
                    if of == OF_PASSKEY {
                        self.delete(passkey_key(rest))
                    } else if of == OF_SESSION {
                        self.delete(session_key(rest))
                    } else if of == OF_CODE {
                        self.delete(code_key(rest))
                    } else if of == OF_TOKEN {
                        self.delete(token_key(rest))
                    } else if of == OF_RUN && rest.len() == 8 {
                        self.delete(run_key(u64_at(rest, 0)))
                    } else if of == OF_BEST {
                        if let Some(b) = read::<Best>(e.value) {
                            self.delete(b.ranked.clone())
                        }
                    }
                    self.delete(e.key.clone())
                }
                if es.len() == 256 {
                    // A scan now would be answered before these deletes commit, and find them
                    // again: the next is made in the next call, after a byte asked for.
                    self.random(1, Step::DeleteNext, take j)
                    return
                }
                self.delete(name_key(a.name))
                self.delete(account_key(a.id))
                self.session_gone(conn)
                self.reply(conn, Reply::Done)
            },
            Step::UploadToken => {
                let t: Option<GameToken> = got(answer)
                let Some(t) = t else {
                    self.reply(
                        conn,
                        Reply::Rejected { why: String::from("Sign in at the console to upload.") },
                    )
                    return
                }
                if t.expires < self.now || t.game.as_str() != self.game.id() {
                    self.reply(
                        conn,
                        Reply::Rejected {
                            why: String::from("Sign in at the console again to upload."),
                        },
                    )
                    return
                }
                for other in self.jobs {
                    if other.id == t.account && is_upload(other.step) {
                        self.reply(
                            conn,
                            Reply::Rejected { why: String::from("One upload at a time.") },
                        )
                        return
                    }
                }
                j.id = t.account
                self.get(account_key(t.account), Step::UploadAccount, take j)
            },
            Step::UploadAccount => {
                let a: Option<Account> = got(answer)
                let Some(a) = a else {
                    self.reply(
                        conn,
                        Reply::Rejected { why: String::from("That account is gone.") },
                    )
                    return
                }
                if a.deleting {
                    self.reply(
                        conn,
                        Reply::Rejected { why: String::from("That account is gone.") },
                    )
                    return
                }
                j.account = Some(a.clone())
                self.get(rate_key(a.id, self.now / HOUR), Step::UploadRate, take j)
            },
            Step::UploadRate => {
                var count: u32 = 0
                if let Some(v) = value(answer) {
                    if v.len() == 4 {
                        count = u32_at(v, 0)
                    }
                }
                if count >= RUNS_AN_HOUR {
                    self.reply(
                        conn,
                        Reply::Rejected {
                            why: String::from(
                                f"At most {RUNS_AN_HOUR} uploads an hour. Try again later.",
                            ),
                        },
                    )
                    return
                }
                j.n = count
                self.get(upload_key(j.id, j.message), Step::UploadSeen, take j)
            },
            Step::UploadSeen => {
                if value(answer).is_some() {
                    self.reply(
                        conn,
                        Reply::Rejected { why: String::from("That run is already uploaded.") },
                    )
                    return
                }
                self.scan(queue_prefix(), MOST_QUEUED + 1, Step::UploadQueue, take j)
            },
            Step::UploadQueue => {
                let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
                if es.len() >= MOST_QUEUED {
                    self.reply(
                        conn,
                        Reply::Rejected {
                            why: String::from("The boards are busy. Try again in a few minutes."),
                        },
                    )
                    return
                }
                self.random(8, Step::UploadId, take j)
            },
            Step::UploadId => {
                let Some(a) = j.account.clone() else { return }
                if answer.len() < 8 {
                    return
                }
                // A run's number is never 0: 0 is a whole game's place.
                let id = max(u64_at(answer, 0), 1)
                let Request::Upload { replay, .. } = j.request.clone() else { return }
                var count: Vec<u8> = Vec::new()
                append_u32(mut count, j.n + 1)
                self.put_bytes(rate_key(a.id, self.now / HOUR), take count)
                self.put_bytes(upload_key(a.id, replay), Vec::new())
                let q = Queued {
                    id,
                    account: a.id,
                    name: names::text(a.name),
                    game: String::from(self.game.id()),
                    board: self.game.board(),
                    course: j.category,
                    ticks: j.tries,
                    uploaded: self.now,
                    replay: replay.clone(),
                }
                self.put(queue_key(self.now, id), q)
                self.queue_waiting = true
                self.queue_written = self.call
                // Answered when its run is.
                self.uploads.push((conn, id))
            },
            Step::BoardScan => {
                let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
                let Request::Board { course, .. } = j.request.clone() else { return }
                var places: Vec<Place> = Vec::new()
                for k in j.n..min(es.len(), j.n + BOARD_PAGE) {
                    borrow e = es[k]
                    let Some(r) = read::<Ranked>(e.value) else { continue }
                    // The key ends with the time and the account.
                    let ticks = u32_at(e.key, e.key.len() - 12)
                    let run = if course == WHOLE { 0 } else { r.run }
                    places.push(Place { place: k + 1, name: r.name.clone(), ticks, run })
                }
                self.reply(conn, Reply::Board { places, total: es.len() })
            },
            Step::WatchRun => {
                let r: Option<Run> = got(answer)
                let Some(r) = r else {
                    self.refuse(conn, "That run is gone.")
                    return
                }
                self.reply(
                    conn,
                    Reply::Run { run: r.id, game: r.game.clone(), replay: r.replay.clone() },
                )
            },
            Step::QueueAccount => {
                self.queue_scan = None
                let Some(q) = j.queued.clone() else { return }
                let a: Option<Account> = got(answer)
                let gone = match a {
                    Some(a) => a.deleting,
                    None => true,
                }
                if gone {
                    self.delete(j.keys[0].clone())
                    self.queue_written = self.call
                    return
                }
                let run = self.game.start(q.replay)
                self.verifying = Some(Verifying { key: j.keys[0].clone(), queued: q.clone(), run })
            },
            Step::FinishBest => self.finish_best(take j, answer),
            Step::FinishBests => self.finish_bests(take j, answer),
            Step::FinishPlace => {
                let Some(q) = j.queued.clone() else { return }
                let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
                // The places ahead, and this one.
                let place = es.len() + 1
                self.tell(q.id, Reply::Verified { run: q.id, ticks: j.tries, place })
            },
        }
    }

    /// A name drawn again: the old one let go, the new one the account's.
    fn renamed(mut self, job: take Job, n: Name) {
        let j = take job
        let Some(a) = j.account.clone() else { return }
        var b = a.clone()
        b.name = n
        b.rerolls = a.rerolls - 1
        self.delete(name_key(a.name))
        self.put_bytes(name_key(n), save(a.id))
        remember(mut self.recent_names, name_key(n))
        self.put(account_key(a.id), b.clone())
        self.set_me(j.conn, me_of(b, recovery: false))
        self.welcome(j.conn)
    }

    /// Ends an export's part once it is long enough, or `last`: the part asked for (`category`) is
    /// the answer, and the export stops there (true); one before it is let go, and counted (`tries`).
    fn export_flush(mut self, job: mut Job, last: bool) -> bool {
        if job.text.len() < EXPORT_PART && !last {
            return false
        }
        if job.tries == job.category || last {
            self.reply(job.conn, Reply::Export { text: job.text.clone(), last })
            return true
        }
        job.tries += 1
        job.text = String::new()
        false
    }

    fn export_next_run(mut self, job: take Job) {
        var j = take job
        if j.keys.is_empty() {
            j.text.push_str("]}")
            let _ = self.export_flush(mut j, last: true)
            return
        }
        let k = j.keys.remove(0)
        self.get(take k, Step::ExportRun, take j)
    }

    // ---- verification -------------------------------------------------------------------------

    /// Plays the run being verified a call's share, or takes the oldest from the queue.
    fn verify_some(mut self) {
        var taken = replace(mut self.verifying, None)
        match mut taken {
            Some(v) => {
                match self.game.play(mut v.run, PLAY_TICKS) {
                    None => {
                        // More to play: something must call again.
                        self.nudge_next()
                        self.verifying = take taken
                    },
                    Some(result) => {
                        self.delete(v.key.clone())
                        self.queue_waiting = true
                        self.queue_written = self.call
                        self.played(v.queued.clone(), result)
                    },
                }
            },
            None => {
                if self.queue_waiting && self.queue_scan.is_none() {
                    if self.call <= self.queue_written {
                        // The queue was written this call: read it in the next, which a byte
                        // asked for brings at once.
                        self.nudge_next()
                        return
                    }
                    let t = self.next_ticket()
                    let from = queue_prefix()
                    let to = past(from).unwrap_or(Vec::new())
                    self.out.push(Command::Scan { ticket: t, from, to, limit: 1, down: false })
                    self.queue_scan = Some(t)
                }
            },
        }
    }

    /// Asks the host for a byte, so that it calls again at once (a room is called when something
    /// happens, and an answer is something).
    fn nudge_next(mut self) {
        if self.nudge.is_none() {
            let t = self.next_ticket()
            self.out.push(Command::Random { ticket: t, n: 1 })
            self.nudge = Some(t)
        }
    }

    fn queue_answered(mut self, answer: Option<Vec<u8>>) {
        let Some(bytes) = answer else { return }
        let Some(es) = entries(bytes) else { return }
        if es.is_empty() {
            self.queue_waiting = false
            return
        }
        borrow e = es[0]
        let Some(q) = read::<Queued>(e.value) else {
            // What can't be read can't be verified.
            self.delete(e.key.clone())
            self.queue_written = self.call
            return
        }
        if q.board != self.game.board() || q.game.as_str() != self.game.id() {
            self.delete(e.key.clone())
            self.queue_written = self.call
            self.tell(
                q.id,
                Reply::Rejected {
                    why: String::from("That run is for another version of the game."),
                },
            )
            return
        }
        // A run whose account went while it waited goes with it.
        var job = blank_job(0, Request::Watch { run: q.id })
        job.queued = Some(q.clone())
        job.keys.push(e.key.clone())
        let t = self.next_ticket()
        self.out.push(Command::Get { ticket: t, key: account_key(q.account) })
        job.ticket = t
        job.step = Step::QueueAccount
        self.jobs.push(take job)
        self.queue_scan = Some(0)
    }

    /// A run played to its end: refused, or kept and ranked.
    fn played(mut self, q: Queued, result: Result<Outcome, Text>) {
        match result {
            Err(why) => self.tell(q.id, Reply::Rejected { why: String::from(why) }),
            Ok(o) => {
                if o.ticks != q.ticks {
                    self.tell(
                        q.id,
                        Reply::Rejected {
                            why: String::from("That run's time isn't what its moves make."),
                        },
                    )
                    return
                }
                let r = Run {
                    id: q.id,
                    account: q.account,
                    game: q.game.clone(),
                    board: q.board,
                    course: q.course,
                    ticks: o.ticks,
                    full: o.full,
                    uploaded: q.uploaded,
                    replay: q.replay.clone(),
                }
                self.put(run_key(r.id), r.clone())
                var id8: Vec<u8> = Vec::new()
                append_u64(mut id8, r.id)
                self.put(
                    indexed(r.account, OF_RUN, id8),
                    RunIndex {
                        game: r.game.clone(),
                        board: r.board,
                        course: r.course,
                        ticks: r.ticks,
                        full: r.full,
                        uploaded: r.uploaded,
                    },
                )
                var job = blank_job(0, Request::Watch { run: r.id })
                job.queued = Some(q.clone())
                job.tries = o.ticks
                job.categories.push(ANY)
                if o.full {
                    job.categories.push(FULL)
                }
                self.next_best(take job)
            },
        }
    }

    /// The next category of the finished run: read the account's best there.
    fn next_best(mut self, job: take Job) {
        var j = take job
        let Some(q) = j.queued.clone() else { return }
        if j.categories.is_empty() {
            // Ranked: its place on the any% board.
            let from = board_prefix(q.game, q.board, q.course, ANY)
            let to = ranked_key(q.game, q.board, q.course, ANY, j.tries, q.account)
            self.scan_range(take from, take to, MOST_PLACE, Step::FinishPlace, take j)
            return
        }
        j.category = j.categories.remove(0)
        self.get(
            best_key(q.account, q.game, q.board, q.course, j.category),
            Step::FinishBest,
            take j,
        )
    }

    fn finish_best(mut self, job: take Job, answer: Vec<u8>) {
        let j = take job
        let Some(q) = j.queued.clone() else { return }
        let old: Option<Best> = got(answer)
        if let Some(b) = old {
            if b.ticks <= j.tries {
                // Not better than the account's best.
                self.next_best(take j)
                return
            }
            self.delete(b.ranked.clone())
        }
        let ranked = ranked_key(q.game, q.board, q.course, j.category, j.tries, q.account)
        self.put(ranked.clone(), Ranked { name: q.name.clone(), run: q.id })
        self.put(
            best_key(q.account, q.game, q.board, q.course, j.category),
            Best { run: q.id, ticks: j.tries, ranked },
        )
        // A new best changes the whole game's sum: read every best of the account's.
        self.scan(
            bests_prefix(q.account, q.game, q.board),
            4 * self.game.courses() + 4,
            Step::FinishBests,
            take j,
        )
    }

    fn finish_bests(mut self, job: take Job, answer: Vec<u8>) {
        let j = take job
        let Some(q) = j.queued.clone() else { return }
        let Some(es) = entries(answer) else { return }
        // The bests the scan saw are as of before this call's writes: the one just written is
        // this run's.
        var courses: Vec<u32> = Vec::new()
        var sum: u32 = 0
        var whole_old: Option<Best> = None
        let skip = bests_prefix(q.account, q.game, q.board).len()
        for e in es {
            if e.key.len() < skip + 8 {
                continue
            }
            let course = u32_at(e.key, skip)
            let category = u32_at(e.key, skip + 4)
            if category != j.category {
                continue
            }
            let Some(b) = read::<Best>(e.value) else { continue }
            if course == WHOLE {
                whole_old = Some(take b)
            } else if course != q.course {
                courses.push(course)
                sum += b.ticks
            }
        }
        courses.push(q.course)
        sum += j.tries
        if courses.len() == self.game.courses() {
            if let Some(b) = whole_old {
                self.delete(b.ranked.clone())
            }
            let ranked = whole_key(q.game, q.board, j.category, sum, q.account)
            self.put(ranked.clone(), Ranked { name: q.name.clone(), run: 0 })
            self.put(
                best_key(q.account, q.game, q.board, WHOLE, j.category),
                Best { run: 0, ticks: sum, ranked },
            )
        }
        self.next_best(take j)
    }
}

/// Whether `key` is among the keys used lately.
fn lately(keys: [Vec<u8>], key: [u8]) -> bool {
    for k in keys {
        if k == Vec::from(key) {
            return true
        }
    }
    false
}

/// Keeps `key` among the keys used lately, the oldest let go past `MOST_RECENT`.
fn remember(keys: mut Vec<Vec<u8>>, key: take Vec<u8>) {
    if keys.len() >= MOST_RECENT {
        let _ = keys.remove(0)
    }
    keys.push(take key)
}

/// Why a ceremony of `kind` can't be finished: it has expired, or was used.
fn expired(kind: u32) -> Text {
    if kind == REGISTER {
        "That sign-up has expired. Start again."
    } else if kind == SIGN_IN { "That sign-in has expired. Try again." } else {
        "That has expired. Start again."
    }
}

/// Drops the times in `xs` older than `window` before `now`.
fn recent(xs: mut Vec<u64>, now: u64, window: u64) {
    var i = 0
    while i < xs.len() {
        if xs[i] + window <= now {
            let _ = xs.remove(i)
        } else {
            i += 1
        }
    }
}

fn is_upload(step: Step) -> bool {
    step == Step::UploadAccount ||
        step == Step::UploadRate ||
        step == Step::UploadSeen ||
        step == Step::UploadQueue ||
        step == Step::UploadId
}

/// A whole game's board: `b/<board>` with `WHOLE` for its course.
pub fn whole_prefix(game: str, board: u32, category: u32) -> Vec<u8> {
    board_prefix(game, board, WHOLE, category)
}

pub fn whole_key(game: str, board: u32, category: u32, ticks: u32, account: u64) -> Vec<u8> {
    ranked_key(game, board, WHOLE, category, ticks, account)
}

// ---- the export ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

fn quoted(out: mut String, s: str) {
    out.push_str("\"")
    json_text(mut out, s)
    out.push_str("\"")
}

fn export_head(a: Account) -> String {
    var out = String::from(
        "{\"about\":\"Everything wrela.dev keeps of your account. Times are milliseconds of the server's clock.\",",
    )
    out.push_str(f"\"account\":{{\"id\":\"{a.id}\",\"handle\":\"{base64url(a.handle)}\",\"name\":")
    quoted(mut out, names::text(a.name).as_str())
    out.push_str(f",\"name_fixed\":{a.fixed},\"created\":{a.created}}},\"records\":[")
    out
}

/// One of an account's index entries as JSON, after the ones before it.
fn export_entry(out: mut String, of: u8, rest: [u8], value: [u8]) {
    if !out.ends_with("[") {
        out.push_str(",")
    }
    if of == OF_PASSKEY {
        let v = read::<PasskeyView>(value)
        out.push_str(f"{{\"passkey\":\"{base64url(rest)}\"")
        if let Some(v) = v {
            out.push_str(f",\"created\":{v.created},\"used\":{v.used}")
        }
        out.push_str("}")
    } else if of == OF_SESSION {
        let v = read::<SessionView>(value)
        out.push_str(f"{{\"session\":\"{hex(public_id(rest))}\"")
        if let Some(v) = v {
            out.push_str(f",\"created\":{v.created},\"seen\":{v.seen}")
        }
        out.push_str("}")
    } else if of == OF_CODE {
        out.push_str("{\"recovery_code\":\"unused (we keep only its hash)\"}")
    } else if of == OF_RUN {
        let v = read::<RunIndex>(value)
        let id = if rest.len() == 8 { u64_at(rest, 0) } else { 0 }
        out.push_str(f"{{\"run\":\"{id}\"")
        if let Some(v) = v {
            out.push_str(",\"game\":")
            quoted(mut out, v.game.as_str())
            out.push_str(
                f",\"board\":{v.board},\"course\":{v.course},\"ticks\":{v.ticks},\"full\":{v.full},\"uploaded\":{v.uploaded}",
            )
        }
        out.push_str("}")
    } else if of == OF_BEST {
        let v = read::<Best>(value)
        out.push_str("{\"best\":")
        match v {
            Some(b) => out.push_str(f"{{\"run\":\"{b.run}\",\"ticks\":{b.ticks}}}"),
            None => out.push_str("null"),
        }
        out.push_str("}")
    } else if of == OF_TOKEN {
        out.push_str("{\"game_token\":\"(we keep only its hash, until it expires)\"}")
    } else if of == OF_HOUR {
        out.push_str("{\"uploads_this_hour\":\"(a count, for the upload limit)\"}")
    } else if of == OF_SEEN {
        out.push_str(f"{{\"uploaded_replay_sha256\":\"{hex(rest)}\"}}")
    } else {
        out.push_str("{}")
    }
}
